// A refined K within gainFloor of the gain of its X is that gain, so the
// distance does not bound its error: at Accuracy 0 on the unfixed gate K was
// off the 320-bit gain by 9.1e-7 (rv49v 2875 NoScaling false), 1.1e-7 (2367
// true), 2.1e-8 (4539 true) and 8.9e-6 (2291, Q(1 - 69 eps), false) as
// generated on arm64, and 1.8e-7 (2367 false) and 6.6e-7 (4539 true) as
// generated on amd64, where the generator rounds differently. Unfixed, the
// first four fail natively only, the last two on both. The Hewer gain was
// exact on all (Q5SCNX). Nor does a distance within gainTol bound it: rv49v
// 1663 true, 1.46e-6 from that gain at a tolerance of 1.51e-6, was 3.11e-6
// off, natively, over its band 4*ksens = 2.5e-6, to which it is held: under
// -race a distance of 3.83e-7, within gainFloor, leaves K 4.21e-7 off (LLTCSS).
// Under gonum 30740af (HF5PTS) -race leaves 2367 true 2.9e-8 off at
// Accuracy 0: held there to the band max(gainFloor, 4·sens.K) only (owner
// BBN22I).
